          "evidence": "Visually, Center A is the leftmost (lowest x-value) and lowest (lowest y-value) point. Moving right and up, Center B is higher than A, Center C is higher than B, Center D is higher than C, and Center E is the rightmost (highest x-value) and highest (highest y-value) point.",
